venus (Android): restore the DRM format modifier list at its original place in the chain

The Termux Android patch hides VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesListEXT from the device's driver during
vkGetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties2 and re-inserted it at the head of the chain afterwards. The reply is
encoded in chain order and the guest (Mesa venus) decodes it against its own chain, so a reordered chain -
e.g. Zink's [FormatProperties3 -> DrmFormatModifierPropertiesList] - made the guest walk off the end of its
chain and crash (NULL dereference in vn_decode_VkFormatProperties2_pnext). Put it back where it was. (PMB OS)

--- a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
@@ -738,8 +738,11 @@
 
 #if defined(__TERMUX__)
    if (mod_list) {
-      mod_list->pNext = args->pFormatProperties->pNext;
-      args->pFormatProperties->pNext = mod_list;
+      /* put it back where it was, not at the head: the guest decodes the reply chain in its own order */
+      VkBaseOutStructure *prev = (VkBaseOutStructure *)args->pFormatProperties;
+      while (prev->pNext != (VkBaseOutStructure *)mod_list->pNext)
+         prev = prev->pNext;
+      prev->pNext = (VkBaseOutStructure *)mod_list;
    }
 #endif
 }
